-- title:
--   split g2: rank 2 and Cartan from b1+b2
-- statement:
--   All matrices and spans are over $\mathbb R$, and the Lie bracket is $[X,Y]=XY-YX$. The source uses one-based matrix indices. Write $F_{pq}$ for the matrix unit, $J_{pq}=F_{pq}-F_{qp}$ and $Z_{pq}=F_{pq}+F_{qp}$. Here rank means Lie rank, and a Cartan subalgebra means a nilpotent, self-normalizing Lie subalgebra.
--
--   Let $L$ be the real matrix Lie algebra generated by BSplitg2 on PDF page 14; $b_i$ denotes its $i$th displayed matrix. Then
--   $$
--   \operatorname{rank}L=2,\qquad
--   (b_1+b_2,\ 2b_4-b_{10}+3b_{11})\text{ is a basis of a Cartan subalgebra of }L.
--   $$
--   The starting element $b_1+b_2$ is retained. The rank here is Lie rank; no stronger assertion about the type of this Cartan is added.
--
--   The explicit family is asserted to be linearly independent and to span the indicated subalgebra; these properties are conclusions. This records the mathematical assertion accompanying the source output.
-- source:
--   Algorithm to compute the rank and a Cartan subalgebra of a matrix Lie algebra with Mathematica, arXiv:math/0205235v1, PDF p. 15, split g2: rank 2 and Cartan from b1+b2

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Gap48_P15

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P15

attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

-- Reuse Mathlib Matrix and Matrix.single directly. Natural one-based
-- coordinates are restricted to Fin coordinates with Matrix.submatrix.

/-- Split g2 has rank 2 and Cartan basis [b1+b2,2b4-b10+3b11].
Source: PDF p. 15, RankOfSplitg2[{b1+b2}]. This is Lie rank, not split rank. -/
theorem splitG2_b1b2_rank_cartan :
    LieAlgebra.rank ℝ splitG2 = 2 ∧
    isCartanBasisFor splitG2 ![bSplitG2 0 + bSplitG2 1,
      (2 : ℝ) • bSplitG2 3 - bSplitG2 9 + (3 : ℝ) • bSplitG2 10] := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P15
